<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inle Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inle Lake is a freshwater lake in the hills of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a>, Myanmar, at about 880 metres above sea level. It is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/intha">Intha</a> people, who fish with a distinctive leg-rowing style and grow crops on floating gardens. In the past it lay within the Shan state of Yawnghwe (Nyaungshwe), and it is famous for the Phaung Daw Oo pagoda and its annual festival.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inle-lake.jpg" alt="Inle Lake" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marc Veraart from Haarlem, Netherlands · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inle_Lake_(Myanmar).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
